@startuml
title OneDrive Client for Linux - HTTPS / libcurl Interactions

participant "OneDrive Client\nfor Linux" as Client
participant "Local OAuth\ncallback listener" as LocalAuth
participant "Web Browser" as Browser
participant "libcurl" as Curl
participant "Microsoft Identity\nplatform" as Identity
participant "Microsoft Graph API" as Graph
participant "GitHub API" as GitHub

== Standard OAuth token acquisition ==
alt Stored refresh token is available
  Client -> Curl: POST refresh-token grant
  Curl -> Identity: HTTPS token request
  Identity --> Curl: Access token + refreshed token data
  Curl --> Client: Token response
else Device authorisation is configured
  Client -> Curl: Request device code
  Curl -> Identity: HTTPS device-code request
  Identity --> Curl: Device code + verification URI
  Curl --> Client: Device authorisation details
  Client -> Browser: User opens verification URI and enters code
  Browser -> Identity: User authenticates / grants consent
  loop Until authorised, declined or expired
    Client -> Curl: Poll token endpoint
    Curl -> Identity: HTTPS device-code token request
    Identity --> Curl: Pending / error / token response
    Curl --> Client: Poll result
  end
else Interactive authorisation-code flow
  alt Local browser callback is available
    Client -> LocalAuth: Start loopback listener
    Client -> Browser: Open authorisation URL
    Browser -> Identity: User authenticates and grants consent
    note over Browser,Identity
      MFA / Conditional Access, when required,
      is handled by the Microsoft identity flow.
    end note
    Identity --> Browser: Redirect to loopback URI with authorisation code
    Browser -> LocalAuth: GET redirect URI
    LocalAuth --> Client: Authorisation code
  else Manual / automated redirect-URI workflow
    Client -> Browser: Present Microsoft authorisation URL
    Browser -> Identity: User authenticates and grants consent
    Identity --> Browser: Redirect URI containing authorisation code
    Browser --> Client: Redirect URI supplied by user or configured auth workflow
  end
  Client -> Curl: Redeem authorisation code
  Curl -> Identity: HTTPS token request
  Identity --> Curl: Access token + refresh token
  Curl --> Client: Token response
end

note over Client,Identity
  Intune / Microsoft Identity Broker authentication is a separate token-acquisition
  path. After a token is available, Microsoft Graph data operations still use the
  normal HTTP transport path shown below.
end note

== Runtime API communication ==
opt Application version check
  Client -> Curl: Query release information
  Curl -> GitHub: HTTPS API request
  GitHub --> Curl: Release metadata
  Curl --> Client: Version response
end

loop Microsoft OneDrive operations
  Client -> Client: Check access-token expiry
  opt Access token has expired
    Client -> Curl: POST refresh-token grant
    Curl -> Identity: HTTPS token request
    Identity --> Curl: New access token / expiry
    Curl --> Client: Token response
  end
  Client -> Curl: Construct authenticated HTTPS request
  Curl -> Graph: Microsoft Graph API request
  Graph --> Curl: API response / file transfer
  Curl --> Client: Parsed response / transfer result
end
@enduml
